    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-07-21; see the referring visit&apos;s Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Alert and composed; speaks in short stretches because talking aggravates the throat pain</td></tr><tr><td>Oral cavity</td><td>Several restored teeth and gum recession; no lesion of the mouth; opens his mouth fully</td></tr><tr><td>Oropharynx</td><td>Ulcerated, firm lesion of the right tonsillar pillar; the left side is normal</td></tr><tr><td>Flexible laryngoscopy</td><td>Nasopharynx clear; the right tonsillar pillar lesion is seen from above; larynx clear, with both vocal folds moving normally; hypopharynx clear</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>Firm, nontender right level II node, matching the CT; no other nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Procedure</td><td>Biopsy of the right tonsillar pillar lesion under topical anesthesia; minor bleeding stopped with pressure; tissue sent for frozen section, permanent sections, and p16</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
